# Sample for the tests: a plain `go test ./...` checks only these puzzles,
# `STARBATTLE_ALL_HARD=1 go test ./...` all of bibliothek.idx.
# It covers sizes 5 to 14 and every rule (Pigeonhole and DeadCells too, with
# and without lookahead), but leaves out the expensive cases with long
# lookahead chains (mostly N = 14, 3 to 5 s each).
#
# Solved by all rules without lookahead:
n05_s029.txt  # smallest, library no. 1
n08_s087.txt  # many Confinement steps
n11_s059.txt  # many ForcedPartner steps
n12_s005.txt  # DeadCells even without lookahead
#
# Need lookahead even with all rules:
n10_s396.txt  # smallest with lookahead (9 steps)
n11_s095.txt  # Pigeonhole, 11 lookahead steps
n12_s082.txt  # many DeadCells steps, short
n13_s181.txt  # N = 13
n14_s024.txt  # N = 14, the cheapest of that size
